Feature Enhancement Request \f1\u8594?\f0  Implement dynamic / adaptive grid spacing to improve performance in varying volatility regimes (RANGING_CALM vs RANGING_VOLATILE especially)\par
Yes \f2\emdash  making grid spacing dynamic (adjusted based on current volatility) is one of the highest-value upgrades you can make to the GridTradingStrategy. Static spacing works in narrow regimes but underperforms when volatility expands/contracts, leading to:\par
\par
Too-tight grids in high-vol \f1\u8594?\f0  excessive trades, fee bleed, whipsaw losses\par
Too-wide grids in low-vol \f1\u8594?\f0  missed small oscillations, low fill rate\par
\par
Dynamic spacing directly addresses this \f2\emdash  it's a common evolution in production grid bots (ATR-multiplier or Bollinger-based adjustment is standard in 2025\endash 2026 crypto bots).\par
Recommended Approach: ATR-Based Dynamic Spacing\par
Why ATR?\par
\par
Directly measures average price range \f1\u8594?\f0  perfect proxy for "how far can price realistically move before mean-reversion likely kicks in"\par
Already calculated in your codebase (calculate_atr)\par
Regime-aware: high ATR \f1\u8594?\f0  widen spacing (protect against whipsaws), low ATR \f1\u8594?\f0  tighten (capture more oscillations)\par
Simple, low-latency, no extra dependencies\par
\par
Core Rule:\par
textcurrent_spacing = base_spacing_multiplier \'d7 ATR(period=14, timeframe=5m or 15m)\par
\par
base_spacing_multiplier: configurable (e.g. 0.8\f2\endash 2.0)\par
Recalculate spacing periodically (every 15\endash 60 min or on regime shift / new grid signal)\par
Apply to new replenishment legs (existing unfilled orders can optionally be adjusted via recenter)\par
\par
Two Variants to Consider (pick one or make configurable)\par
VariantSpacing FormulaWhen to UseProsConsATR Multiplier (simplest & recommended)spacing = k \f0\'d7 ATR(14)  (k = 0.8\f2\endash 1.8)All ranging regimesFast, robust, volatility-normalizedLinear \emdash  may need k adjustment per symbolBollinger Width Hybridspacing = (BB_upper - BB_lower) / (num_levels \f0\'d7 factor)When you want bands to define the entire rangeNaturally fits mean-reversion zonesSlightly slower calc, more params to tuneVolatility Percentilespacing = base \'d7 (current_ATR / ATR_50th_percentile)Advanced regime filterCaps extreme expansionNeeds historical ATR buffer\par
Start with ATR Multiplier \f2\emdash  it's battle-tested in crypto grid bots.\par
